title: send prints ok -> for a remote @host target when only queued locally (no connector); should report queued + warn
---
c2c send <alias>@<host> prints ok -> ... even when no working connector is live. It only enqueues to the remote-outbox and never delivers, but reads as success. An agent will truthfully but wrongly report sent and move on. Fix: for remote @host targets with no live relay path, report queued (not ok); warn to run c2c relay connect or use relay dm send; surface delivery.state in --json; exit code must let a script detect non-delivery. Distinct from B039/B052 (routing) and B044 (--from). Source: friction-points-cn.md.